@@ -4,12 +4,19 @@ A small team notes app. Next.js App Router + TypeScript + Tailwind.
 
 ## Status
 
-- Users live in `src/lib/users.ts` as an in-memory list.
-- `/dashboard` shows the current user and the team.
-- There is no sign-in, no billing, and no email yet.
+- Auth is [Better Auth](https://better-auth.com): email + password and Google sign-in.
+  Users and sessions live in SQLite (`data/notely.db`); `src/lib/users.ts` reads from it.
+- `/dashboard` is protected by `src/proxy.ts` (and re-checked in the page); signed-out visitors go to `/sign-in`.
+- There is no billing and no email yet (so no email verification or password reset).
 
 ## Develop
 
 ```bash
+cp .env.example .env.local   # then fill in real values (see below)
+npm run db:migrate           # create auth tables (re-run after changing auth plugins)
 npm run dev
 ```
+
+Google: create an OAuth client in Google Cloud Console and add the redirect URI
+`http://localhost:3000/api/auth/callback/google`. Set `BETTER_AUTH_SECRET` with `openssl rand -base64 32`.
+SQLite on local disk suits dev and single-server hosting; use a hosted database for serverless deploys.
